{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01KhBxfSpJomSw4yGmacBSLo","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Rust translation of the C library in `c_src/` — a stripped-down `cute_c2`\n2\t//! 2D collision-detection library.\n3\t//!\n4\t//! Built as a `cdylib`, this crate exports exactly the same 46 dynamic symbols as the\n5\t//! C shared object (verified with `nm -D`: the diff is empty in both directions) and\n6\t//! is byte-for-byte behaviour-compatible with it.\n7\t//!\n8\t//! # Module map\n9\t//!\n10\t//! | module | contents |\n11\t//! |---|---|\n12\t//! | [`types`] | all `repr(C)` structs, layout-verified against GCC |\n13\t//! | [`fp`] | explicit SSE NaN-propagation for commutative `+`/`*` |\n14\t//! | [`math`] | scalar / vector / rotation primitives |\n15\t//! | [`shapes`] | plane extraction, AABB corners, proxies, support map, edge normals |\n16\t//! | [`gjk`] | simplex reduction, witness points, `c2GJK` |\n17\t//! | [`manifold`] | clipping helpers and the per-shape-pair manifold generators |\n18\t//! | [`api`] | `c2Collide`, `ptr_from_parts`, `omni_manifold` |\n19\t//!\n20\t//! The five `static` helpers in the C source (`c2Clip`, `c2SidePlanes`,\n21\t//! `c2SidePlanesFromPoly`, `c2KeepDeep`, `c2Incident`) are private here too, matching\n22\t//! the C library's dynamic symbol table.\n23\t//!\n24\t//! # Achieving bit-exact floating point\n25\t//!\n26\t//! * All arithmetic is `f32`, associated exactly as the C source associates it. GCC\n27\t//!   does not reassociate floating point without `-ffast-math`, and neither toolchain\n28\t//!   enables FMA at the x86-64 baseline (SSE2 only), so the arithmetic agrees exactly.\n29\t//! * Every exported function is `#[inline(never)]`. The C library is built without\n30\t//!   `-fno-semantic-interposition`, so GCC routes *every* public→public call through\n31\t//!   the PLT (e.g. `c2Len` really does `call c2Dot@plt`). Letting LLVM inline these\n32\t//!   instead would change which operand ends up as an instruction's destination, and\n33\t//!   therefore which NaN survives.\n34\t//! * `c2Maxv` / `c2Minv` / `c2Absv` use raw comparisons, not `f32::max` / `f32::min` /\n35\t//!   `f32::abs`: C's ternaries return the *second* operand when the first is NaN, and\n36\t//!   return `-0.0` unchanged, whereas the Rust library functions do neither.\n37\t//! * Commutative `+`/`*` go through [`fp::add`] / [`fp::mul`], which take the SSE\n38\t//!   *destination* operand first. GCC's choice of destination is recorded at each\n39\t//!   site (several are reversed relative to the source order, e.g. `c2Mulvs` is\n40\t//!   vectorised so the broadcast scalar is the destination, and\n41\t//!   `c2AABBtoAABBManifold` adds the extents as `eB + eA`).\n42\t//! * Array indexing that C leaves unchecked is done with raw pointer offsets, so no\n43\t//!   bounds check can panic across the FFI boundary where C would happily read on.\n44\t//!\n45\t//! # Bugs are reproduced, not fixed\n46\t//!\n47\t//! * `c2MakeProxy` and `ptr_from_parts` have no `C2_TYPE_POLY` case and no `default`,\n48\t//!   and `c2Collide` silently ignores polygons. See [`gjk::c2GJK`] and\n49\t//!   [`api::ptr_from_parts`].\n50\t//! * `omni_manifold` leaks both shapes it allocates.\n51\t//!\n52\t//! # Where the C library is not a function of its inputs\n53\t//!\n54\t//! Because `c2MakeProxy` never writes the proxy for `C2_TYPE_POLY`, `c2GJK` reads an\n55\t//! uninitialised `c2Proxy` off its own stack on every polygon path — which includes\n56\t//! `c2CapsuletoPolyManifold`, `c2AABBtoCapsuleManifold` and hence\n57\t//! `omni_manifold`/`c2Collide` for AABB-vs-capsule. Measured against the compiled C\n58\t//! library:\n59\t//!\n60\t//! * Normally that stack region is virgin, zero-filled, so the polygon proxy behaves\n61\t//!   as a single point at the origin with radius 0. This crate reproduces that exact\n62\t//!   behaviour by zero-initialising the proxies — deterministic and non-crashing.\n63\t//! * When the region has been dirtied, the proxy's `count` becomes garbage and\n64\t//!   `c2Support` walks off the end of the array. The C library therefore **segfaults\n65\t//!   in roughly a third of runs** purely as a function of stack layout / ASLR.\n66\t//!\n67\t//! A related case: in `c2CapsuletoPolyManifold` the `if (d > sep)` search leaves\n68\t//! `index` at its initial `~0 == -1` when every candidate is NaN (a degenerate AABB\n69\t//! makes `c2Norms` produce NaN normals), after which C evaluates `p->verts[-1]`, four\n70\t//! bytes *before* the struct. This crate performs the same out-of-bounds read.\n71\t//!\n72\t//! Differential testing against the C `.so` covered ~1.5 M cases — all 46 symbols\n73\t//! over structured corpora, random 32-bit patterns (quiet/signalling NaNs of both\n74\t//! signs with random payloads, infinities, signed zeros, denormals), random\n75\t//! simplices, GJK with and without transforms and with cache round-trips, and\n76\t//! ~440 K `omni_manifold` calls across all 16 type pairs. Output is compared as raw\n77\t//! bytes, so NaN payloads and `-0.0` are included. Every case in which the C library\n78\t//! is a deterministic function of its inputs matches byte for byte.\n79\t\n80\t#![allow(non_snake_case)]\n81\t#![allow(non_camel_case_types)]\n82\t#![allow(non_upper_case_globals)]\n83\t\n84\tpub mod api;\n85\tpub mod fp;\n86\tpub mod gjk;\n87\tpub mod manifold;\n88\tpub mod math;\n89\tpub mod shapes;\n90\tpub mod types;\n91\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"27d6de7a-57e2-4fbc-9590-8efa6a5bf865","uuid":"ae9611bd-4490-4a72-9942-723aacbc26c6","timestamp":"2026-08-20T11:51:12.833Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-4VIOLY/translated_rust/src/lib.rs","content":"//! Rust translation of the C library in `c_src/` — a stripped-down `cute_c2`\n//! 2D collision-detection library.\n//!\n//! Built as a `cdylib`, this crate exports exactly the same 46 dynamic symbols as the\n//! C shared object (verified with `nm -D`: the diff is empty in both directions) and\n//! is byte-for-byte behaviour-compatible with it.\n//!\n//! # Module map\n//!\n//! | module | contents |\n//! |---|---|\n//! | [`types`] | all `repr(C)` structs, layout-verified against GCC |\n//! | [`fp`] | explicit SSE NaN-propagation for commutative `+`/`*` |\n//! | [`math`] | scalar / vector / rotation primitives |\n//! | [`shapes`] | plane extraction, AABB corners, proxies, support map, edge normals |\n//! | [`gjk`] | simplex reduction, witness points, `c2GJK` |\n//! | [`manifold`] | clipping helpers and the per-shape-pair manifold generators |\n//! | [`api`] | `c2Collide`, `ptr_from_parts`, `omni_manifold` |\n//!\n//! The five `static` helpers in the C source (`c2Clip`, `c2SidePlanes`,\n//! `c2SidePlanesFromPoly`, `c2KeepDeep`, `c2Incident`) are private here too, matching\n//! the C library's dynamic symbol table.\n//!\n//! # Achieving bit-exact floating point\n//!\n//! * All arithmetic is `f32`, associated exactly as the C source associates it. GCC\n//!   does not reassociate floating point without `-ffast-math`, and neither toolchain\n//!   enables FMA at the x86-64 baseline (SSE2 only), so the arithmetic agrees exactly.\n//! * Every exported function is `#[inline(never)]`. The C library is built without\n//!   `-fno-semantic-interposition`, so GCC routes *every* public→public call through\n//!   the PLT (e.g. `c2Len` really does `call c2Dot@plt`). Letting LLVM inline these\n//!   instead would change which operand ends up as an instruction's destination, and\n//!   therefore which NaN survives.\n//! * `c2Maxv` / `c2Minv` / `c2Absv` use raw comparisons, not `f32::max` / `f32::min` /\n//!   `f32::abs`: C's ternaries return the *second* operand when the first is NaN, and\n//!   return `-0.0` unchanged, whereas the Rust library functions do neither.\n//! * Commutative `+`/`*` go through [`fp::add`] / [`fp::mul`], which take the SSE\n//!   *destination* operand first. GCC's choice of destination is recorded at each\n//!   site (several are reversed relative to the source order, e.g. `c2Mulvs` is\n//!   vectorised so the broadcast scalar is the destination, and\n//!   `c2AABBtoAABBManifold` adds the extents as `eB + eA`).\n//! * Array indexing that C leaves unchecked is done with raw pointer offsets, so no\n//!   bounds check can panic across the FFI boundary where C would happily read on.\n//!\n//! # Bugs are reproduced, not fixed\n//!\n//! * `c2MakeProxy` and `ptr_from_parts` have no `C2_TYPE_POLY` case and no `default`,\n//!   and `c2Collide` silently ignores polygons. See [`gjk::c2GJK`] and\n//!   [`api::ptr_from_parts`].\n//! * `omni_manifold` leaks both shapes it allocates.\n//!\n//! # Where the C library is not a function of its inputs\n//!\n//! Because `c2MakeProxy` never writes the proxy for `C2_TYPE_POLY`, `c2GJK` reads an\n//! uninitialised `c2Proxy` off its own stack on every polygon path — which includes\n//! `c2CapsuletoPolyManifold`, `c2AABBtoCapsuleManifold` and hence\n//! `omni_manifold`/`c2Collide` for AABB-vs-capsule. Measured against the compiled C\n//! library:\n//!\n//! * Normally that stack region is virgin, zero-filled, so the polygon proxy behaves\n//!   as a single point at the origin with radius 0. This crate reproduces that exact\n//!   behaviour by zero-initialising the proxies — deterministic and non-crashing.\n//! * When the region has been dirtied, the proxy's `count` becomes garbage and\n//!   `c2Support` walks off the end of the array. The C library therefore **segfaults\n//!   in roughly a third of runs** purely as a function of stack layout / ASLR.\n//!\n//! A related case: in `c2CapsuletoPolyManifold` the `if (d > sep)` search leaves\n//! `index` at its initial `~0 == -1` when every candidate is NaN (a degenerate AABB\n//! makes `c2Norms` produce NaN normals), after which C evaluates `p->verts[-1]`, four\n//! bytes *before* the struct. This crate performs the same out-of-bounds read.\n//!\n//! Differential testing against the C `.so` covered ~1.5 M cases — all 46 symbols\n//! over structured corpora, random 32-bit patterns (quiet/signalling NaNs of both\n//! signs with random payloads, infinities, signed zeros, denormals), random\n//! simplices, GJK with and without transforms and with cache round-trips, and\n//! ~440 K `omni_manifold` calls across all 16 type pairs. Output is compared as raw\n//! bytes, so NaN payloads and `-0.0` are included. Every case in which the C library\n//! is a deterministic function of its inputs matches byte for byte.\n\n#![allow(non_snake_case)]\n#![allow(non_camel_case_types)]\n#![allow(non_upper_case_globals)]\n\npub mod api;\npub mod fp;\npub mod gjk;\npub mod manifold;\npub mod math;\npub mod shapes;\npub mod types;\n","numLines":91,"startLine":1,"totalLines":91}}}
