{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_nbbsazjh6jnpxacry5zbodtngduojas2n5ye5u6e4ym4wiri6y2a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The C library **segfaults** in a fresh process on the AABB↔CAPSULE path (exit 139), confirming genuine UB. Let me rewrite the probe to document this, then build the main differential suite."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":272,"cache_read_input_tokens":145075,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":272,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"27d6de7a-57e2-4fbc-9590-8efa6a5bf865","uuid":"abe74b7a-5394-494e-8776-bf9460a5c458","timestamp":"2026-08-20T12:05:45.589Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_nbbsazjh6jnpxacry5zbodtngduojas2n5ye5u6e4ym4wiri6y2a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01T4y7532GNBnazYQ96DWni4","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-4VIOLY/translated_rust/tests/probe_uninit.rs","content":"//! Characterises the *one* place where the C library is not a function of its\n//! inputs, so the rest of the suite knows exactly which inputs it may compare.\n//!\n//! `c2MakeProxy` has no `C2_TYPE_POLY` case and no `default:`, so it writes\n//! **nothing** for a polygon. `c2GJK` declares `c2Proxy pA, pB;` without an\n//! initialiser, therefore every call with `typeA`/`typeB == C2_TYPE_POLY` (or any\n//! out-of-range `C2_TYPE`) reads an **uninitialised stack local**:\n//!\n//! ```c\n//! c2Proxy pA; c2Proxy pB;            /* uninitialised */\n//! c2MakeProxy(A, typeA, &pA);        /* no-op for POLY */\n//! c2MakeProxy(B, typeB, &pB);        /* no-op for POLY */\n//! ...\n//! s.a.sB = c2Mulxv(bx, pB.verts[0]); /* reads garbage       */\n//! int iB = c2Support(pB.verts, pB.count, ...);  /* garbage count -> OOB walk */\n//! ```\n//!\n//! Measured behaviour of the compiled C `.so` (gcc 11.5.0, `cmake` default flags):\n//!\n//! * Called from this Rust test harness, `pB.verts[0]` reads back the low/high\n//!   halves of a **stack address**, e.g. `(824111500000.0, 4.56e-41)` ==\n//!   `0x00007f3b_533fe0e0`, so `c2GJK` returns a nonsense distance around `8.2e11`.\n//!   The exact value changes with ASLR from run to run.\n//! * Called from a minimal fresh-process C driver (`dlopen` + one\n//!   `omni_manifold(AABB, CAPSULE)` call) the garbage `pB.count` makes `c2Support`\n//!   walk off the end of the array and the process dies with **SIGSEGV (exit 139),\n//!   reproducibly**.\n//!\n//! So for these inputs the C library has no defined behaviour and *no* translation\n//! can be byte-identical to it. `src/gjk.rs` therefore zero-initialises both\n//! proxies, which reproduces the \"virgin, zero-filled stack page\" case: a POLY\n//! operand behaves as a single point at the origin with radius 0. That is\n//! deterministic, non-crashing, and is asserted below.\n//!\n//! ## Which inputs are affected\n//!\n//! | entry point | affected when |\n//! |---|---|\n//! | `c2GJK` | `typeA` or `typeB` is `C2_TYPE_POLY` or out of range |\n//! | `c2CapsuletoPolyManifold` | **always** (it calls `c2GJK` with `C2_TYPE_POLY`) |\n//! | `c2AABBtoCapsuleManifold` | **always** (promotes the AABB to a `c2Poly`) |\n//! | `c2Collide` / `omni_manifold` | pairs `(AABB, CAPSULE)` and `(CAPSULE, AABB)` |\n//!\n//! Every other entry point and every other type pair *is* a pure function of its\n//! inputs and is compared byte-for-byte by the `phase_b_*` / `phase_c_*` suites.\n\nmod common;\nuse common::*;\nuse std::ffi::c_void;\n\n/// Deliberately dirty the stack below the current frame with a recognisable pattern.\n#[inline(never)]\nfn dirty_stack(depth: u32) -> u64 {\n    let mut buf = [0u64; 96];\n    for (i, b) in buf.iter_mut().enumerate() {\n        *b = 0xDEAD_BEEF_CAFE_0000u64 | (i as u64) | ((depth as u64) << 32);\n    }\n    let mut acc = std::hint::black_box(&buf).iter().fold(0u64, |a, b| a ^ b);\n    if depth > 0 {\n        acc ^= dirty_stack(depth - 1);\n    }\n    std::hint::black_box(acc)\n}\n\nfn gjk_poly(f: &libloading::Symbol<'_, FnGJK>, cap: &c2Capsule, poly: &c2Poly) -> (f32, c2v, c2v, i32) {\n    let (mut a, mut b, mut it) = (poison_v(1), poison_v(2), -12345i32);\n    let d = unsafe {\n        f(\n            cap as *const c2Capsule as *const c_void,\n            C2_TYPE_CAPSULE,\n            std::ptr::null(),\n            poly as *const c2Poly as *const c_void,\n            C2_TYPE_POLY,\n            std::ptr::null(),\n            &mut a,\n            &mut b,\n            0,\n            &mut it,\n            std::ptr::null_mut(),\n        )\n    };\n    (d, a, b, it)\n}\n\n/// The Rust side implements the zero-proxy model: a POLY operand behaves as the\n/// single point (0,0) with radius 0, so `c2GJK(capsule, POLY)` returns the distance\n/// from the capsule *segment* to the origin with `outB == (0,0)`.\n#[test]\nfn rust_poly_operand_is_the_zero_proxy() {\n    let l = libs();\n    let (_cf, rf) = l.get::<FnGJK>(\"c2GJK\");\n\n    // Closest point of the segment [(3,4),(5,6)] to (0,0) is (3,4), distance 5.\n    let cap = c2Capsule { a: v(3.0, 4.0), b: v(5.0, 6.0), r: 1.0 };\n    let mut poly = c2Poly::default();\n    poly.count = 5;\n    for i in 0..5 {\n        poly.verts[i] = v(10.0 + i as f32, 20.0 - i as f32);\n    }\n\n    let (rd, ra, rb, rit) = gjk_poly(&rf, &cap, &poly);\n    assert_eq!(rd, 5.0, \"Rust must report the segment-to-origin distance\");\n    assert_eq!(ra, v(3.0, 4.0), \"witness on A\");\n    assert_eq!(rb, v(0.0, 0.0), \"witness on B is the origin (zero proxy)\");\n    assert_eq!(rit, 0, \"terminates immediately\");\n}\n\n/// ...and it is *deterministic*: the same inputs give the same bytes no matter how\n/// dirty the stack below the caller's frame is. This is exactly the property the C\n/// library lacks.\n#[test]\nfn rust_poly_operand_is_deterministic_under_dirty_stack() {\n    let l = libs();\n    let (_cf, rf) = l.get::<FnGJK>(\"c2GJK\");\n    let cap = c2Capsule { a: v(3.0, 4.0), b: v(5.0, 6.0), r: 1.0 };\n    let poly = c2Poly::default();\n\n    let reference = gjk_poly(&rf, &cap, &poly);\n    for depth in [0u32, 1, 4, 16, 40] {\n        let sink = dirty_stack(depth);\n        let got = gjk_poly(&rf, &cap, &poly);\n        assert_eq!(\n            (got.0.to_bits(), got.1, got.2, got.3),\n            (reference.0.to_bits(), reference.1, reference.2, reference.3),\n            \"Rust c2GJK(POLY) changed after dirtying the stack (depth {depth}, sink {sink:x})\"\n        );\n    }\n}\n\n/// Document, rather than assert, the C library's garbage: print what it returns so\n/// the divergence is on the record, and prove it is *not* a function of its inputs\n/// by showing the same inputs give a value derived from a stack address.\n#[test]\nfn c_poly_operand_reads_uninitialised_stack() {\n    let l = libs();\n    let (cf, _rf) = l.get::<FnGJK>(\"c2GJK\");\n    let cap = c2Capsule { a: v(3.0, 4.0), b: v(5.0, 6.0), r: 1.0 };\n    let poly = c2Poly::default();\n\n    let (cd, ca, cb, cit) = gjk_poly(&cf, &cap, &poly);\n    println!(\"C   c2GJK(CAPSULE, POLY) -> d={cd} outA={ca:?} outB={cb:?} iters={cit}\");\n    println!(\"    outB bits = (0x{:08x}, 0x{:08x})\", cb.x.to_bits(), cb.y.to_bits());\n    println!(\"    -> reinterpreted as one 64-bit little-endian word: 0x{:016x}\",\n        ((cb.y.to_bits() as u64) << 32) | cb.x.to_bits() as u64);\n    println!(\"    a stack address on this machine looks like 0x00007f........\");\n\n    // The witness point on A is still correct (pA *is* initialised for a capsule),\n    // which pinpoints pB as the uninitialised operand.\n    assert_eq!(ca, v(3.0, 4.0), \"pA is initialised, so outA is meaningful\");\n\n    // No assertion on `cd` / `cb`: they are indeterminate. This test exists to\n    // document the UB, not to pin it down.\n    let _ = (cd, cb, cit);\n}\n\n/// Rust must never crash on the POLY path, however the polygon is shaped --\n/// including `count` values far outside 0..=8.\n#[test]\nfn rust_poly_path_never_crashes() {\n    let l = libs();\n    let (_cf, rf) = l.get::<FnGJK>(\"c2GJK\");\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(0x5EED_1234);\n    for trial in 0..200 {\n        let cap = c2Capsule { a: rng.vec_mixed(20.0), b: rng.vec_mixed(20.0), r: rng.f_mixed(3.0) };\n        let mut poly = c2Poly::default();\n        poly.count = match trial % 5 {\n            0 => 0,\n            1 => -7,\n            2 => 8,\n            3 => 4,\n            _ => rng.below(9) as i32,\n        };\n        for i in 0..8 {\n            poly.verts[i] = rng.vec_mixed(10.0);\n            poly.norms[i] = rng.vec_mixed(1.0);\n        }\n        let (mut a, mut b, mut it) = (c2v::default(), c2v::default(), 0i32);\n        let d = unsafe {\n            rf(\n                &cap as *const c2Capsule as *const c_void,\n                C2_TYPE_CAPSULE,\n                std::ptr::null(),\n                &poly as *const c2Poly as *const c_void,\n                C2_TYPE_POLY,\n                std::ptr::null(),\n                &mut a,\n                &mut b,\n                0,\n                &mut it,\n                std::ptr::null_mut(),\n            )\n        };\n        // Just needs to return; assert the out params were written at all.\n        assert!(it >= 0 && it <= 20, \"trial {trial}: iterations out of range: {it}\");\n        let _ = (d, a, b);\n    }\n}\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":272,"cache_read_input_tokens":145075,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":272,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"27d6de7a-57e2-4fbc-9590-8efa6a5bf865","uuid":"41948b5c-3640-49a2-97e0-702b7b245e57","timestamp":"2026-08-20T12:06:25.732Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01T4y7532GNBnazYQ96DWni4","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-4VIOLY/translated_rust/tests/probe_uninit.rs has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"27d6de7a-57e2-4fbc-9590-8efa6a5bf865","uuid":"1f045523-cd11-4293-84ce-0d89d982bb19","timestamp":"2026-08-20T12:06:25.749Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-4VIOLY/translated_rust/tests/probe_uninit.rs","content":"//! Characterises the *one* place where the C library is not a function of its\n//! inputs, so the rest of the suite knows exactly which inputs it may compare.\n//!\n//! `c2MakeProxy` has no `C2_TYPE_POLY` case and no `default:`, so it writes\n//! **nothing** for a polygon. `c2GJK` declares `c2Proxy pA, pB;` without an\n//! initialiser, therefore every call with `typeA`/`typeB == C2_TYPE_POLY` (or any\n//! out-of-range `C2_TYPE`) reads an **uninitialised stack local**:\n//!\n//! ```c\n//! c2Proxy pA; c2Proxy pB;            /* uninitialised */\n//! c2MakeProxy(A, typeA, &pA);        /* no-op for POLY */\n//! c2MakeProxy(B, typeB, &pB);        /* no-op for POLY */\n//! ...\n//! s.a.sB = c2Mulxv(bx, pB.verts[0]); /* reads garbage       */\n//! int iB = c2Support(pB.verts, pB.count, ...);  /* garbage count -> OOB walk */\n//! ```\n//!\n//! Measured behaviour of the compiled C `.so` (gcc 11.5.0, `cmake` default flags):\n//!\n//! * Called from this Rust test harness, `pB.verts[0]` reads back the low/high\n//!   halves of a **stack address**, e.g. `(824111500000.0, 4.56e-41)` ==\n//!   `0x00007f3b_533fe0e0`, so `c2GJK` returns a nonsense distance around `8.2e11`.\n//!   The exact value changes with ASLR from run to run.\n//! * Called from a minimal fresh-process C driver (`dlopen` + one\n//!   `omni_manifold(AABB, CAPSULE)` call) the garbage `pB.count` makes `c2Support`\n//!   walk off the end of the array and the process dies with **SIGSEGV (exit 139),\n//!   reproducibly**.\n//!\n//! So for these inputs the C library has no defined behaviour and *no* translation\n//! can be byte-identical to it. `src/gjk.rs` therefore zero-initialises both\n//! proxies, which reproduces the \"virgin, zero-filled stack page\" case: a POLY\n//! operand behaves as a single point at the origin with radius 0. That is\n//! deterministic, non-crashing, and is asserted below.\n//!\n//! ## Which inputs are affected\n//!\n//! | entry point | affected when |\n//! |---|---|\n//! | `c2GJK` | `typeA` or `typeB` is `C2_TYPE_POLY` or out of range |\n//! | `c2CapsuletoPolyManifold` | **always** (it calls `c2GJK` with `C2_TYPE_POLY`) |\n//! | `c2AABBtoCapsuleManifold` | **always** (promotes the AABB to a `c2Poly`) |\n//! | `c2Collide` / `omni_manifold` | pairs `(AABB, CAPSULE)` and `(CAPSULE, AABB)` |\n//!\n//! Every other entry point and every other type pair *is* a pure function of its\n//! inputs and is compared byte-for-byte by the `phase_b_*` / `phase_c_*` suites.\n\nmod common;\nuse common::*;\nuse std::ffi::c_void;\n\n/// Deliberately dirty the stack below the current frame with a recognisable pattern.\n#[inline(never)]\nfn dirty_stack(depth: u32) -> u64 {\n    let mut buf = [0u64; 96];\n    for (i, b) in buf.iter_mut().enumerate() {\n        *b = 0xDEAD_BEEF_CAFE_0000u64 | (i as u64) | ((depth as u64) << 32);\n    }\n    let mut acc = std::hint::black_box(&buf).iter().fold(0u64, |a, b| a ^ b);\n    if depth > 0 {\n        acc ^= dirty_stack(depth - 1);\n    }\n    std::hint::black_box(acc)\n}\n\nfn gjk_poly(f: &libloading::Symbol<'_, FnGJK>, cap: &c2Capsule, poly: &c2Poly) -> (f32, c2v, c2v, i32) {\n    let (mut a, mut b, mut it) = (poison_v(1), poison_v(2), -12345i32);\n    let d = unsafe {\n        f(\n            cap as *const c2Capsule as *const c_void,\n            C2_TYPE_CAPSULE,\n            std::ptr::null(),\n            poly as *const c2Poly as *const c_void,\n            C2_TYPE_POLY,\n            std::ptr::null(),\n            &mut a,\n            &mut b,\n            0,\n            &mut it,\n            std::ptr::null_mut(),\n        )\n    };\n    (d, a, b, it)\n}\n\n/// The Rust side implements the zero-proxy model: a POLY operand behaves as the\n/// single point (0,0) with radius 0, so `c2GJK(capsule, POLY)` returns the distance\n/// from the capsule *segment* to the origin with `outB == (0,0)`.\n#[test]\nfn rust_poly_operand_is_the_zero_proxy() {\n    let l = libs();\n    let (_cf, rf) = l.get::<FnGJK>(\"c2GJK\");\n\n    // Closest point of the segment [(3,4),(5,6)] to (0,0) is (3,4), distance 5.\n    let cap = c2Capsule { a: v(3.0, 4.0), b: v(5.0, 6.0), r: 1.0 };\n    let mut poly = c2Poly::default();\n    poly.count = 5;\n    for i in 0..5 {\n        poly.verts[i] = v(10.0 + i as f32, 20.0 - i as f32);\n    }\n\n    let (rd, ra, rb, rit) = gjk_poly(&rf, &cap, &poly);\n    assert_eq!(rd, 5.0, \"Rust must report the segment-to-origin distance\");\n    assert_eq!(ra, v(3.0, 4.0), \"witness on A\");\n    assert_eq!(rb, v(0.0, 0.0), \"witness on B is the origin (zero proxy)\");\n    assert_eq!(rit, 0, \"terminates immediately\");\n}\n\n/// ...and it is *deterministic*: the same inputs give the same bytes no matter how\n/// dirty the stack below the caller's frame is. This is exactly the property the C\n/// library lacks.\n#[test]\nfn rust_poly_operand_is_deterministic_under_dirty_stack() {\n    let l = libs();\n    let (_cf, rf) = l.get::<FnGJK>(\"c2GJK\");\n    let cap = c2Capsule { a: v(3.0, 4.0), b: v(5.0, 6.0), r: 1.0 };\n    let poly = c2Poly::default();\n\n    let reference = gjk_poly(&rf, &cap, &poly);\n    for depth in [0u32, 1, 4, 16, 40] {\n        let sink = dirty_stack(depth);\n        let got = gjk_poly(&rf, &cap, &poly);\n        assert_eq!(\n            (got.0.to_bits(), got.1, got.2, got.3),\n            (reference.0.to_bits(), reference.1, reference.2, reference.3),\n            \"Rust c2GJK(POLY) changed after dirtying the stack (depth {depth}, sink {sink:x})\"\n        );\n    }\n}\n\n/// Document, rather than assert, the C library's garbage: print what it returns so\n/// the divergence is on the record, and prove it is *not* a function of its inputs\n/// by showing the same inputs give a value derived from a stack address.\n#[test]\nfn c_poly_operand_reads_uninitialised_stack() {\n    let l = libs();\n    let (cf, _rf) = l.get::<FnGJK>(\"c2GJK\");\n    let cap = c2Capsule { a: v(3.0, 4.0), b: v(5.0, 6.0), r: 1.0 };\n    let poly = c2Poly::default();\n\n    let (cd, ca, cb, cit) = gjk_poly(&cf, &cap, &poly);\n    println!(\"C   c2GJK(CAPSULE, POLY) -> d={cd} outA={ca:?} outB={cb:?} iters={cit}\");\n    println!(\"    outB bits = (0x{:08x}, 0x{:08x})\", cb.x.to_bits(), cb.y.to_bits());\n    println!(\"    -> reinterpreted as one 64-bit little-endian word: 0x{:016x}\",\n        ((cb.y.to_bits() as u64) << 32) | cb.x.to_bits() as u64);\n    println!(\"    a stack address on this machine looks like 0x00007f........\");\n\n    // The witness point on A is still correct (pA *is* initialised for a capsule),\n    // which pinpoints pB as the uninitialised operand.\n    assert_eq!(ca, v(3.0, 4.0), \"pA is initialised, so outA is meaningful\");\n\n    // No assertion on `cd` / `cb`: they are indeterminate. This test exists to\n    // document the UB, not to pin it down.\n    let _ = (cd, cb, cit);\n}\n\n/// Rust must never crash on the POLY path, however the polygon is shaped --\n/// including `count` values far outside 0..=8.\n#[test]\nfn rust_poly_path_never_crashes() {\n    let l = libs();\n    let (_cf, rf) = l.get::<FnGJK>(\"c2GJK\");\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(0x5EED_1234);\n    for trial in 0..200 {\n        let cap = c2Capsule { a: rng.vec_mixed(20.0), b: rng.vec_mixed(20.0), r: rng.f_mixed(3.0) };\n        let mut poly = c2Poly::default();\n        poly.count = match trial % 5 {\n            0 => 0,\n            1 => -7,\n            2 => 8,\n            3 => 4,\n            _ => rng.below(9) as i32,\n        };\n        for i in 0..8 {\n            poly.verts[i] = rng.vec_mixed(10.0);\n            poly.norms[i] = rng.vec_mixed(1.0);\n        }\n        let (mut a, mut b, mut it) = (c2v::default(), c2v::default(), 0i32);\n        let d = unsafe {\n            rf(\n                &cap as *const c2Capsule as *const c_void,\n                C2_TYPE_CAPSULE,\n                std::ptr::null(),\n                &poly as *const c2Poly as *const c_void,\n                C2_TYPE_POLY,\n                std::ptr::null(),\n                &mut a,\n                &mut b,\n                0,\n                &mut it,\n                std::ptr::null_mut(),\n            )\n        };\n        // Just needs to return; assert the out params were written at all.\n        assert!(it >= 0 && it <= 20, \"trial {trial}: iterations out of range: {it}\");\n        let _ = (d, a, b);\n    }\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":15,"newStart":1,"newLines":48,"lines":["-//! Probes for the *one* place where the C library is not a pure function of its","-//! inputs: `c2MakeProxy` has no `C2_TYPE_POLY` case, so `c2GJK` reads an","-//! uninitialised `c2Proxy` off its own stack on every polygon path","-//! (`c2CapsuletoPolyManifold` -> `c2AABBtoCapsuleManifold` -> `c2Collide` /","-//! `omni_manifold` for the AABB-vs-CAPSULE pair).","+//! Characterises the *one* place where the C library is not a function of its","+//! inputs, so the rest of the suite knows exactly which inputs it may compare."," //!","-//! These tests establish empirically that, for this build, the region reads back","-//! all-zero — i.e. the polygon proxy behaves as a single point at the origin with","-//! radius 0 — and that this stays true after the stack below the caller's frame has","-//! been deliberately dirtied. That is the model `src/gjk.rs` reproduces by","-//! zero-initialising, and it is what makes ERRORS.