{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_kaqtepq3r3lnct6rq6iugwgujtfrktscwoz6kwnilhptjipvyafq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The release build's optimized stack layout makes the C library's UB actually segfault. Let me isolate that characterization probe into a child process:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":391,"cache_read_input_tokens":393886,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":391,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"27d6de7a-57e2-4fbc-9590-8efa6a5bf865","uuid":"c6717031-e94b-461a-9102-11c6830ab17e","timestamp":"2026-08-20T12:42:03.444Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_kaqtepq3r3lnct6rq6iugwgujtfrktscwoz6kwnilhptjipvyafq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_018DmPFNd2VeurVBzy5j3efy","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-4VIOLY/translated_rust/tests/probe_uninit.rs","content":"//! Characterises the *one* place where the C library is not a function of its\n//! inputs, so the rest of the suite knows exactly which inputs it may compare and\n//! why `common::zero_stack` exists.\n//!\n//! `c2MakeProxy` has no `C2_TYPE_POLY` case and no `default:`, so it writes\n//! **nothing** for a polygon. `c2GJK` declares `c2Proxy pA, pB;` without an\n//! initialiser, therefore every call with `typeA`/`typeB == C2_TYPE_POLY` (or any\n//! out-of-range `C2_TYPE`) reads an **uninitialised stack local**:\n//!\n//! ```c\n//! c2Proxy pA; c2Proxy pB;            /* uninitialised                     */\n//! c2MakeProxy(A, typeA, &pA);        /* no-op for POLY                    */\n//! c2MakeProxy(B, typeB, &pB);        /* no-op for POLY                    */\n//! ...\n//! s.a.sB = c2Mulxv(bx, pB.verts[0]);            /* reads garbage          */\n//! int iB = c2Support(pB.verts, pB.count, ...);  /* garbage count -> OOB   */\n//! ```\n//!\n//! Measured behaviour of the compiled C `.so` (gcc 11.5.0, `cmake` default flags,\n//! i.e. `-O0`):\n//!\n//! * From a debug test binary, `pB.verts[0]` reads back the two halves of a **stack\n//!   address** — e.g. `(0.001952216, 4.5751e-41)` == `0x00007f89_3affe180` — so\n//!   `c2GJK` returns a nonsense distance. The value moves with ASLR from run to run.\n//! * From a minimal fresh-process C driver (`dlopen` + one\n//!   `omni_manifold(AABB, CAPSULE)` call), the garbage `pB.count` makes `c2Support`\n//!   walk off the end of the array and the process dies with **SIGSEGV, exit 139,\n//!   reproducibly**. The same happens from a release-profile test binary, which is\n//!   why the demonstration below runs in a **child process**.\n//!\n//! So for these inputs the C library has no defined behaviour and no translation can\n//! be byte-identical to it. `src/gjk.rs` zero-initialises both proxies, reproducing\n//! the \"virgin, zero-filled stack page\" case: a POLY operand behaves as a single\n//! point at the origin with radius 0. That is deterministic, never crashes, and is\n//! asserted here.\n//!\n//! `common::zero_stack()` forces the C side into that same state, which is what lets\n//! `tests/phase_b_manifolds.rs` and `tests/phase_b_api.rs` compare the polygon paths\n//! byte-for-byte after all (and with them the five `static` helpers `c2Clip`,\n//! `c2SidePlanes`, `c2SidePlanesFromPoly`, `c2KeepDeep`, `c2Incident`, which are\n//! unreachable through any other entry point).\n//!\n//! ## Which inputs are affected\n//!\n//! | entry point | affected when |\n//! |---|---|\n//! | `c2GJK` | `typeA` or `typeB` is `C2_TYPE_POLY` or out of range |\n//! | `c2CapsuletoPolyManifold` | **always** (it calls `c2GJK` with `C2_TYPE_POLY`) |\n//! | `c2AABBtoCapsuleManifold` | **always** (it promotes the AABB to a `c2Poly`) |\n//! | `c2Collide` / `omni_manifold` | pairs `(AABB, CAPSULE)` and `(CAPSULE, AABB)` |\n//!\n//! Every other entry point and every other type pair *is* a pure function of its\n//! inputs and is compared byte-for-byte by the `phase_b_*` / `phase_c_*` suites.\n#![allow(non_snake_case)]\n\nmod common;\nuse common::*;\nuse std::ffi::c_void;\n\n/// Deliberately dirty the stack below the current frame with a recognisable pattern.\n#[inline(never)]\nfn dirty_stack(depth: u32) -> u64 {\n    let mut buf = [0u64; 96];\n    for (i, b) in buf.iter_mut().enumerate() {\n        *b = 0xDEAD_BEEF_CAFE_0000u64 | (i as u64) | ((depth as u64) << 32);\n    }\n    let mut acc = std::hint::black_box(&buf).iter().fold(0u64, |a, b| a ^ b);\n    if depth > 0 {\n        acc ^= dirty_stack(depth - 1);\n    }\n    std::hint::black_box(acc)\n}\n\nfn gjk_poly(\n    f: &libloading::Symbol<'_, FnGJK>,\n    cap: &c2Capsule,\n    poly: &c2Poly,\n) -> (f32, c2v, c2v, i32) {\n    let (mut a, mut b, mut it) = (poison_v(1), poison_v(2), -12345i32);\n    let d = unsafe {\n        f(\n            cap as *const c2Capsule as *const c_void,\n            C2_TYPE_CAPSULE,\n            std::ptr::null(),\n            poly as *const c2Poly as *const c_void,\n            C2_TYPE_POLY,\n            std::ptr::null(),\n            &mut a,\n            &mut b,\n            0,\n            &mut it,\n            std::ptr::null_mut(),\n        )\n    };\n    (d, a, b, it)\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// What the Rust side guarantees\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n/// The Rust side implements the zero-proxy model: a POLY operand behaves as the\n/// single point (0,0) with radius 0, so `c2GJK(capsule, POLY)` returns the distance\n/// from the capsule *segment* to the origin with `outB == (0,0)`.\n#[test]\nfn rust_poly_operand_is_the_zero_proxy() {\n    let l = libs();\n    let (_cf, rf) = l.get::<FnGJK>(\"c2GJK\");\n\n    // Closest point of the segment [(3,4),(5,6)] to (0,0) is (3,4), distance 5.\n    let cap = c2Capsule { a: v(3.0, 4.0), b: v(5.0, 6.0), r: 1.0 };\n    let mut poly = c2Poly::default();\n    poly.count = 5;\n    for i in 0..5 {\n        poly.verts[i] = v(10.0 + i as f32, 20.0 - i as f32);\n    }\n\n    let (rd, ra, rb, rit) = gjk_poly(&rf, &cap, &poly);\n    assert_eq!(rd, 5.0, \"Rust must report the segment-to-origin distance\");\n    assert_eq!(ra, v(3.0, 4.0), \"witness on A\");\n    assert_eq!(rb, v(0.0, 0.0), \"witness on B is the origin (zero proxy)\");\n    assert_eq!(rit, 0, \"terminates immediately\");\n}\n\n/// ...and it is *deterministic*: identical bytes no matter how dirty the stack below\n/// the caller's frame is. This is exactly the property the C library lacks.\n#[test]\nfn rust_poly_operand_is_deterministic_under_dirty_stack() {\n    let l = libs();\n    let (_cf, rf) = l.get::<FnGJK>(\"c2GJK\");\n    let cap = c2Capsule { a: v(3.0, 4.0), b: v(5.0, 6.0), r: 1.0 };\n    let poly = c2Poly::default();\n\n    let reference = gjk_poly(&rf, &cap, &poly);\n    for depth in [0u32, 1, 4, 16, 40] {\n        let sink = dirty_stack(depth);\n        let got = gjk_poly(&rf, &cap, &poly);\n        assert_eq!(\n            (got.0.to_bits(), got.1, got.2, got.3),\n            (reference.0.to_bits(), reference.1, reference.2, reference.3),\n            \"Rust c2GJK(POLY) changed after dirtying the stack (depth {depth}, sink {sink:x})\"\n        );\n    }\n}\n\n/// Rust must never crash on the POLY path, however the polygon is shaped —\n/// including `count` values far outside `0..=8`.\n#[test]\nfn rust_poly_path_never_crashes() {\n    let l = libs();\n    let (_cf, rf) = l.get::<FnGJK>(\"c2GJK\");\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(0x5EED_1234);\n    for trial in 0..200 {\n        let cap = c2Capsule { a: rng.vec_mixed(20.0), b: rng.vec_mixed(20.0), r: rng.f_mixed(3.0) };\n        let mut poly = c2Poly::default();\n        poly.count = match trial % 5 {\n            0 => 0,\n            1 => -7,\n            2 => 8,\n            3 => 4,\n            _ => rng.below(9) as i32,\n        };\n        for i in 0..8 {\n            poly.verts[i] = rng.vec_mixed(10.0);\n            poly.norms[i] = rng.vec_mixed(1.0);\n        }\n        let (d, a, b, it) = gjk_poly(&rf, &cap, &poly);\n        assert!((0..=20).contains(&it), \"trial {trial}: iterations out of range: {it}\");\n        let _ = (d, a, b);\n    }\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// What the C side actually does — demonstrated in a CHILD PROCESS, because the\n// uninitialised `pB.count` can make `c2Support` walk into unmapped memory.\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nconst CHILD_ENV: &str = \"OMNI_UB_CHILD\";\n\n/// Runs in a child process (see [`c_poly_operand_is_undefined_behaviour`]). Calls the\n/// C library on the POLY path with the stack left as-is and prints what came back.\n#[test]\n#[ignore = \"spawned as a child process by c_poly_operand_is_undefined_behaviour\"]\nfn ub_child_calls_c_poly_path() {\n    if std::env::var(CHILD_ENV).is_err() {\n        // Never run this directly: it may SIGSEGV by design.\n        println!(\"SKIPPED (set {CHILD_ENV}=1 to run)\");\n        return;\n    }\n    let l = libs();\n    let (cf, _rf) = l.get::<FnGJK>(\"c2GJK\");\n    let cap = c2Capsule { a: v(3.0, 4.0), b: v(5.0, 6.0), r: 1.0 };\n    let poly = c2Poly::default();\n    // No zero_stack() here -- that is the whole point.\n    let (cd, ca, cb, cit) = gjk_poly(&cf, &cap, &poly);\n    println!(\"RESULT d={} outA=({},{}) outB_bits=(0x{:08x},0x{:08x}) iters={cit}\",\n        cd, ca.x, ca.y, cb.x.to_bits(), cb.y.to_bits());\n    // pA *is* initialised for a capsule, so outA stays meaningful -- which pinpoints\n    // pB as the uninitialised operand.\n    assert_eq!(ca, v(3.0, 4.0), \"pA is initialised, so outA must be meaningful\");\n    if cd == 5.0 && cb.x == 0.0 && cb.y == 0.0 {\n        println!(\"VERDICT zero-proxy (this run's stack happened to be zero-filled)\");\n    } else {\n        println!(\"VERDICT garbage (uninitialised stack observed)\");\n    }\n}\n\n/// Demonstrates that the C library's POLY path is **not** a function of its inputs:\n/// the child either reports a value derived from an uninitialised stack slot, or dies\n/// with a signal. Both outcomes are recorded; neither is something a translation can\n/// reproduce, which is why `common::zero_stack()` is used everywhere else.\n#[test]\nfn c_poly_operand_is_undefined_behaviour() {\n    use std::process::Command;\n    let exe = std::env::current_exe().expect(\"current_exe\");\n    let out = Command::new(&exe)\n        .args([\"ub_child_calls_c_poly_path\", \"--ignored\", \"--exact\", \"--nocapture\", \"--test-threads=1\"])\n        .env(CHILD_ENV, \"1\")\n        .output()\n        .expect(\"failed to spawn the child test process\");\n\n    let stdout = String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stdout);\n    let stderr = String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stderr);\n    println!(\"child status: {:?}\", out.status);\n    for line in stdout.lines().filter(|l| l.starts_with(\"RESULT\") || l.starts_with(\"VERDICT\")) {\n        println!(\"child: {line}\");\n    }\n\n    let crashed = !out.status.success() && out.status.code().is_none();\n    let garbage = stdout.contains(\"VERDICT garbage\");\n    let zero_proxy = stdout.contains(\"VERDICT zero-proxy\");\n\n    assert!(\n        crashed || garbage || zero_proxy,\n        \"the child neither crashed nor produced a verdict.\\nstdout:\\n{stdout}\\nstderr:\\n{stderr}\"\n    );\n\n    if crashed {\n        println!(\n            \"=> C SIGSEGV'd on the POLY path: the uninitialised `pB.count` made \\\n             c2Support read unmapped memory. Confirms ERRORS.md rows 19/20.\"\n        );\n    } else if garbage {\n        println!(\n            \"=> C returned a value derived from an uninitialised stack slot. \\\n             Confirms ERRORS.md rows 19/20.\"\n        );\n    } else {\n        println!(\n            \"=> C happened to see a zero-filled stack this run, i.e. it agreed with \\\n             the model src/gjk.rs implements. Still UB, just benign here.\"\n        );\n    }\n}\n\n/// With `zero_stack()` applied to both sides the C library agrees with Rust exactly.\n/// This is the property the rest of the suite relies on.\n#[test]\nfn zero_stack_makes_c_agree_with_rust() {\n    let l = libs();\n    let (cf, rf) = l.get::<FnGJK>(\"c2GJK\");\n    let cap = c2Capsule { a: v(3.0, 4.0), b: v(5.0, 6.0), r: 1.0 };\n    let poly = c2Poly::default();\n\n    // Warm up so lazy PLT resolution inside the .so does not dirty the stack during\n    // the measured calls.\n    warmup(|| {\n        zero_stack();\n        let _ = gjk_poly(&cf, &cap, &poly);\n        zero_stack();\n        let _ = gjk_poly(&rf, &cap, &poly);\n    });\n\n    for depth in [0u32, 1, 4, 16, 40] {\n        let _ = dirty_stack(depth);\n        zero_stack();\n        let (cd, ca, cb, cit) = gjk_poly(&cf, &cap, &poly);\n        zero_stack();\n        let (rd, ra, rb, rit) = gjk_poly(&rf, &cap, &poly);\n        let ctx = format!(\"after dirty_stack({depth}) + zero_stack()\");\n        eq_f32(\"c2GJK(POLY) dist\", &ctx, cd, rd);\n        eq(\"c2GJK(POLY) outA\", &ctx, &ca, &ra);\n        eq(\"c2GJK(POLY) outB\", &ctx, &cb, &rb);\n        eq_i32(\"c2GJK(POLY) iters\", &ctx, cit, rit);\n        assert_eq!(cd, 5.0, \"with a zeroed stack the C side sees the zero proxy\");\n    }\n}\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":391,"cache_read_input_tokens":393886,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":391,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"27d6de7a-57e2-4fbc-9590-8efa6a5bf865","uuid":"ac5f68b2-bb06-4a09-94cd-8743315a67c1","timestamp":"2026-08-20T12:42:54.922Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_018DmPFNd2VeurVBzy5j3efy","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-4VIOLY/translated_rust/tests/probe_uninit.rs has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"27d6de7a-57e2-4fbc-9590-8efa6a5bf865","uuid":"32bdcb95-9e76-4af7-b015-13ee1db54521","timestamp":"2026-08-20T12:42:54.937Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-4VIOLY/translated_rust/tests/probe_uninit.rs","content":"//! Characterises the *one* place where the C library is not a function of its\n//! inputs, so the rest of the suite knows exactly which inputs it may compare and\n//! why `common::zero_stack` exists.\n//!\n//! `c2MakeProxy` has no `C2_TYPE_POLY` case and no `default:`, so it writes\n//! **nothing** for a polygon. `c2GJK` declares `c2Proxy pA, pB;` without an\n//! initialiser, therefore every call with `typeA`/`typeB == C2_TYPE_POLY` (or any\n//! out-of-range `C2_TYPE`) reads an **uninitialised stack local**:\n//!\n//! ```c\n//! c2Proxy pA; c2Proxy pB;            /* uninitialised                     */\n//! c2MakeProxy(A, typeA, &pA);        /* no-op for POLY                    */\n//! c2MakeProxy(B, typeB, &pB);        /* no-op for POLY                    */\n//! ...\n//! s.a.sB = c2Mulxv(bx, pB.verts[0]);            /* reads garbage          */\n//! int iB = c2Support(pB.verts, pB.count, ...);  /* garbage count -> OOB   */\n//! ```\n//!\n//! Measured behaviour of the compiled C `.so` (gcc 11.5.0, `cmake` default flags,\n//! i.e. `-O0`):\n//!\n//! * From a debug test binary, `pB.verts[0]` reads back the two halves of a **stack\n//!   address** — e.g. `(0.001952216, 4.5751e-41)` == `0x00007f89_3affe180` — so\n//!   `c2GJK` returns a nonsense distance. The value moves with ASLR from run to run.\n//! * From a minimal fresh-process C driver (`dlopen` + one\n//!   `omni_manifold(AABB, CAPSULE)` call), the garbage `pB.count` makes `c2Support`\n//!   walk off the end of the array and the process dies with **SIGSEGV, exit 139,\n//!   reproducibly**. The same happens from a release-profile test binary, which is\n//!   why the demonstration below runs in a **child process**.\n//!\n//! So for these inputs the C library has no defined behaviour and no translation can\n//! be byte-identical to it. `src/gjk.rs` zero-initialises both proxies, reproducing\n//! the \"virgin, zero-filled stack page\" case: a POLY operand behaves as a single\n//! point at the origin with radius 0. That is deterministic, never crashes, and is\n//! asserted here.\n//!\n//! `common::zero_stack()` forces the C side into that same state, which is what lets\n//! `tests/phase_b_manifolds.rs` and `tests/phase_b_api.rs` compare the polygon paths\n//! byte-for-byte after all (and with them the five `static` helpers `c2Clip`,\n//! `c2SidePlanes`, `c2SidePlanesFromPoly`, `c2KeepDeep`, `c2Incident`, which are\n//! unreachable through any other entry point).\n//!\n//! ## Which inputs are affected\n//!\n//! | entry point | affected when |\n//! |---|---|\n//! | `c2GJK` | `typeA` or `typeB` is `C2_TYPE_POLY` or out of range |\n//! | `c2CapsuletoPolyManifold` | **always** (it calls `c2GJK` with `C2_TYPE_POLY`) |\n//! | `c2AABBtoCapsuleManifold` | **always** (it promotes the AABB to a `c2Poly`) |\n//! | `c2Collide` / `omni_manifold` | pairs `(AABB, CAPSULE)` and `(CAPSULE, AABB)` |\n//!\n//! Every other entry point and every other type pair *is* a pure function of its\n//! inputs and is compared byte-for-byte by the `phase_b_*` / `phase_c_*` suites.\n#![allow(non_snake_case)]\n\nmod common;\nuse common::*;\nuse std::ffi::c_void;\n\n/// Deliberately dirty the stack below the current frame with a recognisable pattern.\n#[inline(never)]\nfn dirty_stack(depth: u32) -> u64 {\n    let mut buf = [0u64; 96];\n    for (i, b) in buf.iter_mut().enumerate() {\n        *b = 0xDEAD_BEEF_CAFE_0000u64 | (i as u64) | ((depth as u64) << 32);\n    }\n    let mut acc = std::hint::black_box(&buf).iter().fold(0u64, |a, b| a ^ b);\n    if depth > 0 {\n        acc ^= dirty_stack(depth - 1);\n    }\n    std::hint::black_box(acc)\n}\n\nfn gjk_poly(\n    f: &libloading::Symbol<'_, FnGJK>,\n    cap: &c2Capsule,\n    poly: &c2Poly,\n) -> (f32, c2v, c2v, i32) {\n    let (mut a, mut b, mut it) = (poison_v(1), poison_v(2), -12345i32);\n    let d = unsafe {\n        f(\n            cap as *const c2Capsule as *const c_void,\n            C2_TYPE_CAPSULE,\n            std::ptr::null(),\n            poly as *const c2Poly as *const c_void,\n            C2_TYPE_POLY,\n            std::ptr::null(),\n            &mut a,\n            &mut b,\n            0,\n            &mut it,\n            std::ptr::null_mut(),\n        )\n    };\n    (d, a, b, it)\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// What the Rust side guarantees\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n/// The Rust side implements the zero-proxy model: a POLY operand behaves as the\n/// single point (0,0) with radius 0, so `c2GJK(capsule, POLY)` returns the distance\n/// from the capsule *segment* to the origin with `outB == (0,0)`.\n#[test]\nfn rust_poly_operand_is_the_zero_proxy() {\n    let l = libs();\n    let (_cf, rf) = l.get::<FnGJK>(\"c2GJK\");\n\n    // Closest point of the segment [(3,4),(5,6)] to (0,0) is (3,4), distance 5.\n    let cap = c2Capsule { a: v(3.0, 4.0), b: v(5.0, 6.0), r: 1.0 };\n    let mut poly = c2Poly::default();\n    poly.count = 5;\n    for i in 0..5 {\n        poly.verts[i] = v(10.0 + i as f32, 20.0 - i as f32);\n    }\n\n    let (rd, ra, rb, rit) = gjk_poly(&rf, &cap, &poly);\n    assert_eq!(rd, 5.0, \"Rust must report the segment-to-origin distance\");\n    assert_eq!(ra, v(3.0, 4.0), \"witness on A\");\n    assert_eq!(rb, v(0.0, 0.0), \"witness on B is the origin (zero proxy)\");\n    assert_eq!(rit, 0, \"terminates immediately\");\n}\n\n/// ...and it is *deterministic*: identical bytes no matter how dirty the stack below\n/// the caller's frame is. This is exactly the property the C library lacks.\n#[test]\nfn rust_poly_operand_is_deterministic_under_dirty_stack() {\n    let l = libs();\n    let (_cf, rf) = l.get::<FnGJK>(\"c2GJK\");\n    let cap = c2Capsule { a: v(3.0, 4.0), b: v(5.0, 6.0), r: 1.0 };\n    let poly = c2Poly::default();\n\n    let reference = gjk_poly(&rf, &cap, &poly);\n    for depth in [0u32, 1, 4, 16, 40] {\n        let sink = dirty_stack(depth);\n        let got = gjk_poly(&rf, &cap, &poly);\n        assert_eq!(\n            (got.0.to_bits(), got.1, got.2, got.3),\n            (reference.0.to_bits(), reference.1, reference.2, reference.3),\n            \"Rust c2GJK(POLY) changed after dirtying the stack (depth {depth}, sink {sink:x})\"\n        );\n    }\n}\n\n/// Rust must never crash on the POLY path, however the polygon is shaped —\n/// including `count` values far outside `0..=8`.\n#[test]\nfn rust_poly_path_never_crashes() {\n    let l = libs();\n    let (_cf, rf) = l.get::<FnGJK>(\"c2GJK\");\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(0x5EED_1234);\n    for trial in 0..200 {\n        let cap = c2Capsule { a: rng.vec_mixed(20.0), b: rng.vec_mixed(20.0), r: rng.f_mixed(3.0) };\n        let mut poly = c2Poly::default();\n        poly.count = match trial % 5 {\n            0 => 0,\n            1 => -7,\n            2 => 8,\n            3 => 4,\n            _ => rng.below(9) as i32,\n        };\n        for i in 0..8 {\n            poly.verts[i] = rng.vec_mixed(10.0);\n            poly.norms[i] = rng.vec_mixed(1.0);\n        }\n        let (d, a, b, it) = gjk_poly(&rf, &cap, &poly);\n        assert!((0..=20).contains(&it), \"trial {trial}: iterations out of range: {it}\");\n        let _ = (d, a, b);\n    }\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// What the C side actually does — demonstrated in a CHILD PROCESS, because the\n// uninitialised `pB.count` can make `c2Support` walk into unmapped memory.\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nconst CHILD_ENV: &str = \"OMNI_UB_CHILD\";\n\n/// Runs in a child process (see [`c_poly_operand_is_undefined_behaviour`]). Calls the\n/// C library on the POLY path with the stack left as-is and prints what came back.\n#[test]\n#[ignore = \"spawned as a child process by c_poly_operand_is_undefined_behaviour\"]\nfn ub_child_calls_c_poly_path() {\n    if std::env::var(CHILD_ENV).is_err() {\n        // Never run this directly: it may SIGSEGV by design.\n        println!(\"SKIPPED (set {CHILD_ENV}=1 to run)\");\n        return;\n    }\n    let l = libs();\n    let (cf, _rf) = l.get::<FnGJK>(\"c2GJK\");\n    let cap = c2Capsule { a: v(3.0, 4.0), b: v(5.0, 6.0), r: 1.0 };\n    let poly = c2Poly::default();\n    // No zero_stack() here -- that is the whole point.\n    let (cd, ca, cb, cit) = gjk_poly(&cf, &cap, &poly);\n    println!(\"RESULT d={} outA=({},{}) outB_bits=(0x{:08x},0x{:08x}) iters={cit}\",\n        cd, ca.x, ca.y, cb.x.to_bits(), cb.y.to_bits());\n    // pA *is* initialised for a capsule, so outA stays meaningful -- which pinpoints\n    // pB as the uninitialised operand.\n    assert_eq!(ca, v(3.0, 4.0), \"pA is initialised, so outA must be meaningful\");\n    if cd == 5.0 && cb.x == 0.0 && cb.y == 0.0 {\n        println!(\"VERDICT zero-proxy (this run's stack happened to be zero-filled)\");\n    } else {\n        println!(\"VERDICT garbage (uninitialised stack observed)\");\n    }\n}\n\n/// Demonstrates that the C library's POLY path is **not** a function of its inputs:\n/// the child either reports a value derived from an uninitialised stack slot, or dies\n/// with a signal. Both outcomes are recorded; neither is something a translation can\n/// reproduce, which is why `common::zero_stack()` is used everywhere else.\n#[test]\nfn c_poly_operand_is_undefined_behaviour() {\n    use std::process::Command;\n    let exe = std::env::current_exe().expect(\"current_exe\");\n    let out = Command::new(&exe)\n        .args([\"ub_child_calls_c_poly_path\", \"--ignored\", \"--exact\", \"--nocapture\", \"--test-threads=1\"])\n        .env(CHILD_ENV, \"1\")\n        .output()\n        .expect(\"failed to spawn the child test process\");\n\n    let stdout = String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stdout);\n    let stderr = String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stderr);\n    println!(\"child status: {:?}\", out.status);\n    for line in stdout.lines().filter(|l| l.starts_with(\"RESULT\") || l.starts_with(\"VERDICT\")) {\n        println!(\"child: {line}\");\n    }\n\n    let crashed = !out.status.success() && out.status.code().is_none();\n    let garbage = stdout.contains(\"VERDICT garbage\");\n    let zero_proxy = stdout.contains(\"VERDICT zero-proxy\");\n\n    assert!(\n        crashed || garbage || zero_proxy,\n        \"the child neither crashed nor produced a verdict.\\nstdout:\\n{stdout}\\nstderr:\\n{stderr}\"\n    );\n\n    if crashed {\n        println!(\n            \"=> C SIGSEGV'd on the POLY path: the uninitialised `pB.count` made \\\n             c2Support read unmapped memory. Confirms ERRORS.md rows 19/20.\"\n        );\n    } else if garbage {\n        println!(\n            \"=> C returned a value derived from an uninitialised stack slot. \\\n             Confirms ERRORS.md rows 19/20.\"\n        );\n    } else {\n        println!(\n            \"=> C happened to see a zero-filled stack this run, i.e. it agreed with \\\n             the model src/gjk.rs implements. Still UB, just benign here.\"\n        );\n    }\n}\n\n/// With `zero_stack()` applied to both sides the C library agrees with Rust exactly.\n/// This is the property the rest of the suite relies on.\n#[test]\nfn zero_stack_makes_c_agree_with_rust() {\n    let l = libs();\n    let (cf, rf) = l.get::<FnGJK>(\"c2GJK\");\n    let cap = c2Capsule { a: v(3.0, 4.0), b: v(5.0, 6.0), r: 1.0 };\n    let poly = c2Poly::default();\n\n    // Warm up so lazy PLT resolution inside the .so does not dirty the stack during\n    // the measured calls.\n    warmup(|| {\n        zero_stack();\n        let _ = gjk_poly(&cf, &cap, &poly);\n        zero_stack();\n        let _ = gjk_poly(&rf, &cap, &poly);\n    });\n\n    for depth in [0u32, 1, 4, 16, 40] {\n        let _ = dirty_stack(depth);\n        zero_stack();\n        let (cd, ca, cb, cit) = gjk_poly(&cf, &cap, &poly);\n        zero_stack();\n        let (rd, ra, rb, rit) = gjk_poly(&rf, &cap, &poly);\n        let ctx = format!(\"after dirty_stack({depth}) + zero_stack()\");\n        eq_f32(\"c2GJK(POLY) dist\", &ctx, cd, rd);\n        eq(\"c2GJK(POLY) outA\", &ctx, &ca, &ra);\n        eq(\"c2GJK(POLY) outB\", &ctx, &cb, &rb);\n        eq_i32(\"c2GJK(POLY) iters\", &ctx, cit, rit);\n        assert_eq!(cd, 5.0, \"with a zeroed stack the C side sees the zero proxy\");\n    }\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":5,"newStart":1,"newLines":6,"lines":[" //! Characterises the *one* place where the C library is not a function of its","-//! inputs, so the rest of the suite knows exactly which inputs it may compare.","+//! inputs, so the rest of the suite knows exactly which inputs it may compare and","+//! why `common::zero_stack` exists."," //!"," //! `c2MakeProxy` has no `C2_TYPE_POLY` case and no `default:`, so it writes"," //! **nothing** for a polygon. `c2GJK` declares `c2Proxy pA, pB;` without an"]},{"oldStart":7,"oldLines":42,"newStart":8,"newLines":50,"lines":[" //! out-of-range `C2_TYPE`) reads an **uninitialised stack local**:"," //!"," //! ```c","-//! c2Proxy pA; c2Proxy pB;            /* uninitialised */","-//! c2MakeProxy(A, typeA, &pA);        /* no-op for POLY */","-//! c2MakeProxy(B, typeB, &pB);        /* no-op for POLY */","+//! c2Proxy pA; c2Proxy pB;            /* uninitialised                     */","+//! c2MakeProxy(A, typeA, &pA);        /* no-op for POLY                    */","+//! c2MakeProxy(B, typeB, &pB);        /* no-op for POLY                    */"," //! ...","-//! s.a.sB = c2Mulxv(bx, pB.verts[0]); /* reads garbage       */","-//! int iB = c2Support(pB.verts, pB.count, ...);  /* garbage count -> OOB walk */","+//! s.a.sB = c2Mulxv(bx, pB.verts[0]);            /* reads garbage          */","+//! int iB = c2Support(pB.verts, pB.count, ...);  /* garbage count -> OOB   */"," //! ```"," //!","-//! Measured behaviour of the compiled C `.so` (gcc 11.5.0, `cmake` default flags):","+//! Measured behaviour of the compiled C `.so` (gcc 11.5.0, `cmake` default flags,","+//! i.e. `-O0`):"," //!","-//! * Called from this Rust test harness, `pB.verts[0]` reads back the low/high","-//!   halves of a **stack address**, e.g. `(824111500000.0, 4.56e-41)` ==","-//!   `0x00007f3b_533fe0e0`, so `c2GJK` returns a nonsense distance around `8.2e11`.","-//!   The exact value changes with ASLR from run to run.","-//! * Called from a minimal fresh-process C driver (`dlopen` + one","-//!   `omni_manifold(AABB, CAPSULE)` call) the garbage `pB.count` makes `c2Support`","-//!   walk off the end of the array and the process dies with **SIGSEGV (exit 139),","-//!   reproducibly**.","+//! * From a debug test binary, `pB.verts[0]` reads back the two halves of a **stack","+//!   address** — e.g. `(0.001952216, 4.5751e-41)` == `0x00007f89_3affe180` — so","+//!   `c2GJK` returns a nonsense distance. The value moves with ASLR from run to run.","+//! * From a minimal fresh-process C driver (`dlopen` + one","+//!   `omni_manifold(AABB, CAPSULE)` call), the garbage `pB.count` makes `c2Support`","+//!   walk off the end of the array and the process dies with **SIGSEGV, exit 139,","+//!   reproducibly**. The same happens from a release-profile test binary, which is","+//!   why the demonstration below runs in a **child process**."," //!","-//! So for these inputs the C library has no defined behaviour and *no* translation","-//! can be byte-identical to it. `src/gjk.rs` therefore zero-initialises both","-//! proxies, which reproduces the \"virgin, zero-filled stack page\" case: a POLY","-//! operand behaves as a single point at the origin with radius 0. That is","-//! deterministic, non-crashing, and is asserted below.","+//! So for these inputs the C library has no defined behaviour and no translation can","+//! be byte-identical to it. `src/gjk.rs` zero-initialises both proxies, reproducing","+//! the \"virgin, zero-filled stack page\" case: a POLY operand behaves as a single","+//! point at the origin with radius 0. That is deterministic, never crashes, and is","+//! asserted here."," //!","+//! `common::zero_stack()` forces the C side into that same state, which is what lets","+//! `tests/phase_b_manifolds.rs` and `tests/phase_b_api.rs` compare the polygon paths","+//! byte-for-byte after all (and with them the five `static` helpers `c2Clip`,","+//! `c2SidePlanes`, `c2SidePlanesFromPoly`, `c2KeepDeep`, `c2Incident`, which are","+//! unreachable through any other entry point).","+//!"," //! ## Which inputs are affected"," //!"," //! | entry point | affected when |"," //! |---|---|"," //! | `c2GJK` | `typeA` or `typeB` is `C2_TYPE_POLY` or out of range |"," //! | `c2CapsuletoPolyManifold` | **always** (it calls `c2GJK` with `C2_TYPE_POLY`) |","-//! | `c2AABBtoCapsuleManifold` | **always** (promotes the AABB to a `c2Poly`) |","+//! | `c2AABBtoCapsuleManifold` | **always** (it promotes the AABB to a `c2Poly`) |"," //! | `c2Collide` / `omni_manifold` | pairs `(AABB, CAPSULE)` and `(CAPSULE, AABB)` |"," //!"," //! Every other entry point and every other type pair *is* a pure function of its"," //! inputs and is compared byte-for-byte by the `phase_b_*` / `phase_c_*` suites.","+#![allow(non_snake_case)]"," "," mod common;"," use common::*;"]},{"oldStart":62,"oldLines":7,"newStart":71,"newLines":11,"lines":["     std::hint::black_box(acc)"," }"," ","-fn gjk_poly(f: &libloading::Symbol<'_, FnGJK>, cap: &c2Capsule, poly: &c2Poly) -> (f32, c2v, c2v, i32) {","+fn gjk_poly(","+    f: &libloading::Symbol<'_, FnGJK>,","+    cap: &c2Capsule,","+    poly: &c2Poly,","+) -> (f32, c2v, c2v, i32) {","     let (mut a, mut b, mut it) = (poison_v(1), poison_v(2), -12345i32);","     let d = unsafe {","         f("]},{"oldStart":82,"oldLines":6,"newStart":95,"newLines":10,"lines":["     (d, a, b, it)"," }"," ","+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------","+// What the Rust side guarantees","+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------","+"," /// The Rust side implements the zero-proxy model: a POLY operand behaves as the"," /// single point (0,0) with radius 0, so `c2GJK(capsule, POLY)` returns the distance"," /// from the capsule *segment* to the origin with `outB == (0,0)`."]},{"oldStart":105,"oldLines":9,"newStart":122,"newLines":8,"lines":["     assert_eq!(rit, 0, \"terminates immediately\");"," }"," ","-/// ...and it is *deterministic*: the same inputs give the same bytes no matter how","-/// dirty the stack below the caller's frame is. This is exactly the property the C","-/// library lacks.","+/// ...and it is *deterministic*: identical bytes no matter how dirty the stack below","+/// the caller's frame is. This is exactly the property the C library lacks."," #[test]"," fn rust_poly_operand_is_deterministic_under_dirty_stack() {","     let l = libs();"]},{"oldStart":127,"oldLines":35,"newStart":143,"newLines":9,"lines":["     }"," }"," ","-/// Document, rather than assert, the C library's garbage: print what it returns so","-/// the divergence is on the record, and prove it is *not* a function of its inputs","-/// by showing the same inputs give a value derived from a stack address.","+/// Rust must never crash on the POLY path, however the polygon is shaped —","+/// including `count` values far outside `0..=8`."," #[test]","-fn c_poly_operand_reads_uninitialised_stack() {","-    let l = libs();","-    let (cf, _rf) = l.get::<FnGJK>(\"c2GJK\");","-    let cap = c2Capsule { a: v(3.0, 4.0), b: v(5.0, 6.0), r: 1.0 };","-    let poly = c2Poly::default();","-","-    let (cd, ca, cb, cit) = gjk_poly(&cf, &cap, &poly);","-    println!(\"C   c2GJK(CAPSULE, POLY) -> d={cd} outA={ca:?} outB={cb:?} iters={cit}\");","-    println!(\"    outB bits = (0x{:08x}, 0x{:08x})\", cb.x.to_bits(), cb.y.to_bits());","-    println!(\"    -> reinterpreted as one 64-bit little-endian word: 0x{:016x}\",","-        ((cb.y.to_bits() as u64) << 32) | cb.x.to_bits() as u64);","-    println!(\"    a stack address on this machine looks like 0x00007f........\");","-","-    // The witness point on A is still correct (pA *is* initialised for a capsule),","-    // which pinpoints pB as the uninitialised operand.","-    assert_eq!(ca, v(3.0, 4.0), \"pA is initialised, so outA is meaningful\");","-","-    // No assertion on `cd` / `cb`: they are indeterminate. This test exists to","-    // document the UB, not to pin it down.","-    let _ = (cd, cb, cit);","-}","-","-/// Rust must never crash on the POLY path, however the polygon is shaped --","-/// including `count` values far outside 0..=8.","-#[test]"," fn rust_poly_path_never_crashes() {","     let l = libs();","     let (_cf, rf) = l.get::<FnGJK>(\"c2GJK\");"]},{"oldStart":174,"oldLines":24,"newStart":164,"newLines":124,"lines":["             poly.verts[i] = rng.vec_mixed(10.0);","             poly.norms[i] = rng.vec_mixed(1.0);","         }","-        let (mut a, mut b, mut it) = (c2v::default(), c2v::default(), 0i32);","-        let d = unsafe {","-            rf(","-                &cap as *const c2Capsule as *const c_void,","-                C2_TYPE_CAPSULE,","-                std::ptr::null(),","-                &poly as *const c2Poly as *const c_void,","-                C2_TYPE_POLY,","-                std::ptr::null(),","-                &mut a,","-                &mut b,","-                0,","-                &mut it,","-                std::ptr::null_mut(),","-            )","-        };","-        // Just needs to return; assert the out params were written at all.","-        assert!(it >= 0 && it <= 20, \"trial {trial}: iterations out of range: {it}\");","+        let (d, a, b, it) = gjk_poly(&rf, &cap, &poly);","+        assert!((0..=20).contains(&it), \"trial {trial}: iterations out of range: {it}\");","         let _ = (d, a, b);","     }"," }","+","+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------","+// What the C side actually does — demonstrated in a CHILD PROCESS, because the","+// uninitialised `pB.count` can make `c2Support` walk into unmapped memory.","+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------","+","+const CHILD_ENV: &str = \"OMNI_UB_CHILD\";","+","+/// Runs in a child process (see [`c_poly_operand_is_undefined_behaviour`]). Calls the","+/// C library on the POLY path with the stack left as-is and prints what came back.","+#[test]","+#[ignore = \"spawned as a child process by c_poly_operand_is_undefined_behaviour\"]","+fn ub_child_calls_c_poly_path() {","+    if std::env::var(CHILD_ENV).is_err() {","+        // Never run this directly: it may SIGSEGV by design.","+        println!(\"SKIPPED (set {CHILD_ENV}=1 to run)\");","+        return;","+    }","+    let l = libs();","+    let (cf, _rf) = l.get::<FnGJK>(\"c2GJK\");","+    let cap = c2Capsule { a: v(3.0, 4.0), b: v(5.0, 6.0), r: 1.0 };","+    let poly = c2Poly::default();","+    // No zero_stack() here -- that is the whole point.","+    let (cd, ca, cb, cit) = gjk_poly(&cf, &cap, &poly);","+    println!(\"RESULT d={} outA=({},{}) outB_bits=(0x{:08x},0x{:08x}) iters={cit}\",","+        cd, ca.x, ca.y, cb.x.to_bits(), cb.y.to_bits());","+    // pA *is* initialised for a capsule, so outA stays meaningful -- which pinpoints","+    // pB as the uninitialised operand.","+    assert_eq!(ca, v(3.0, 4.0), \"pA is initialised, so outA must be meaningful\");","+    if cd == 5.0 && cb.x == 0.0 && cb.y == 0.0 {","+        println!(\"VERDICT zero-proxy (this run's stack happened to be zero-filled)\");","+    } else {","+        println!(\"VERDICT garbage (uninitialised stack observed)\");","+    }","+}","+","+/// Demonstrates that the C library's POLY path is **not** a function of its inputs:","+/// the child either reports a value derived from an uninitialised stack slot, or dies","+/// with a signal. Both outcomes are recorded; neither is something a translation can","+/// reproduce, which is why `common::zero_stack()` is used everywhere else.","+#[test]","+fn c_poly_operand_is_undefined_behaviour() {","+    use std::process::Command;","+    let exe = std::env::current_exe().expect(\"current_exe\");","+    let out = Command::new(&exe)","+        .args([\"ub_child_calls_c_poly_path\", \"--ignored\", \"--exact\", \"--nocapture\", \"--test-threads=1\"])","+        .env(CHILD_ENV, \"1\")","+        .output()","+        .expect(\"failed to spawn the child test process\");","+","+    let stdout = String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stdout);","+    let stderr = String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stderr);","+    println!(\"child status: {:?}\", out.status);","+    for line in stdout.lines().filter(|l| l.starts_with(\"RESULT\") || l.starts_with(\"VERDICT\")) {","+        println!(\"child: {line}\");","+    }","+","+    let crashed = !out.status.success() && out.status.code().is_none();","+    let garbage = stdout.contains(\"VERDICT garbage\");","+    let zero_proxy = stdout.contains(\"VERDICT zero-proxy\");","+","+    assert!(","+        crashed || garbage || zero_proxy,","+        \"the child neither crashed nor produced a verdict.\\nstdout:\\n{stdout}\\nstderr:\\n{stderr}\"","+    );","+","+    if crashed {","+        println!(","+            \"=> C SIGSEGV'd on the POLY path: the uninitialised `pB.count` made \\","+             c2Support read unmapped memory. Confirms ERRORS.md rows 19/20.\"","+        );","+    } else if garbage {","+        println!(","+            \"=> C returned a value derived from an uninitialised stack slot. \\","+             Confirms ERRORS.md rows 19/20.\"","+        );","+    } else {","+        println!(","+            \"=> C happened to see a zero-filled stack this run, i.e. it agreed with \\","+             the model src/gjk.rs implements. Still UB, just benign here.\"","+        );","+    }","+}","+","+/// With `zero_stack()` applied to both sides the C library agrees with Rust exactly.","+/// This is the property the rest of the suite relies on.","+#[test]","+fn zero_stack_makes_c_agree_with_rust() {","+    let l = libs();","+    let (cf, rf) = l.get::<FnGJK>(\"c2GJK\");","+    let cap = c2Capsule { a: v(3.0, 4.0), b: v(5.0, 6.0), r: 1.0 };","+    let poly = c2Poly::default();","+","+    // Warm up so lazy PLT resolution inside the .so does not dirty the stack during","+    // the measured calls.","+    warmup(|| {","+        zero_stack();","+        let _ = gjk_poly(&cf, &cap, &poly);","+        zero_stack();","+        let _ = gjk_poly(&rf, &cap, &poly);","+    });","+","+    for depth in [0u32, 1, 4, 16, 40] {","+        let _ = dirty_stack(depth);","+        zero_stack();","+        let (cd, ca, cb, cit) = gjk_poly(&cf, &cap, &poly);","+        zero_stack();","+        let (rd, ra, rb, rit) = gjk_poly(&rf, &cap, &poly);","+        let ctx = format!(\"after dirty_stack({depth}) + zero_stack()\");","+        eq_f32(\"c2GJK(POLY) dist\", &ctx, cd, rd);","+        eq(\"c2GJK(POLY) outA\", &ctx, &ca, &ra);","+        eq(\"c2GJK(POLY) outB\", &ctx, &cb, &rb);","+        eq_i32(\"c2GJK(POLY) iters\", &ctx, cit, rit);","+        assert_eq!(cd, 5.0, \"with a zeroed stack the C side sees the zero proxy\");","+    }","+}"]}],"originalFile":"//! Characterises the *one* place where the C library is not a function of its\n//! inputs, so the rest of the suite knows exactly which inputs it may compare.\n//!\n//! `c2MakeProxy` has no `C2_TYPE_POLY` case and no `default:`, so it writes\n//! **nothing** for a polygon. `c2GJK` declares `c2Proxy pA, pB;` without an\n//! initialiser, therefore every call with `typeA`/`typeB == C2_TYPE_POLY` (or any\n//! out-of-range `C2_TYPE`) reads an **uninitialised stack local**:\n//!\n//! ```c\n//! c2Proxy pA; c2Proxy pB;            /* uninitialised */\n//! c2MakeProxy(A, typeA, &pA);        /* no-op for POLY */\n//! c2MakeProxy(B, typeB, &pB);        /* no-op for POLY */\n//! ...\n//! s.a.sB = c2Mulxv(bx, pB.verts[0]); /* reads garbage       */\n//! int iB = c2Support(pB.verts, pB.count, ...);  /* garbage count -> OOB walk */\n//! ```\n//!\n//! Measured behaviour of the compiled C `.so` (gcc 11.5.0, `cmake` default flags):\n//!\n//! * Called from this Rust test harness, `pB.verts[0]` reads back the low/high\n//!   halves of a **stack address**, e.g. `(824111500000.0, 4.56e-41)` ==\n//!   `0x00007f3b_533fe0e0`, so `c2GJK` returns a nonsense distance around `8.2e11`.\n//!   The exact value changes with ASLR from run to run.\n//! * Called from a minimal fresh-process C driver (`dlopen` + one\n//!   `omni_manifold(AABB, CAPSULE)` call) the garbage `pB.count` makes `c2Support`\n//!   walk off the end of the array and the process dies with **SIGSEGV (exit 139),\n//!   reproducibly**.\n//!\n//! So for these inputs the C library has no defined behaviour and *no* translation\n//! can be byte-identical to it. `src/gjk.rs` therefore zero-initialises both\n//! proxies, which reproduces the \"virgin, zero-filled stack page\" case: a POLY\n//! operand behaves as a single point at the origin with radius 0. That is\n//! deterministic, non-crashing, and is asserted below.\n//!\n//! ## Which inputs are affected\n//!\n//! | entry point | affected when |\n//! |---|---|\n//! | `c2GJK` | `typeA` or `typeB` is `C2_TYPE_POLY` or out of range |\n//! | `c2CapsuletoPolyManifold` | **always** (it calls `c2GJK` with `C2_TYPE_POLY`) |\n//! | `c2AABBtoCapsuleManifold` | **always** (promotes the AABB to a `c2Poly`) |\n//! | `c2Collide` / `omni_manifold` | pairs `(AABB, CAPSULE)` and `(CAPSULE, AABB)` |\n//!\n//! Every other entry point and every other type pair *is* a pure function of its\n//! inputs and is compared byte-for-byte by the `phase_b_*` / `phase_c_*` suites.\n\nmod common;\nuse common::*;\nuse std::ffi::c_void;\n\n/// Deliberately dirty the stack below the current frame with a recognisable pattern.\n#[inline(never)]\nfn dirty_stack(depth: u32) -> u64 {\n    let mut buf = [0u64; 96];\n    for (i, b) in buf.iter_mut().enumerate() {\n        *b = 0xDEAD_BEEF_CAFE_0000u64 | (i as u64) | ((depth as u64) << 32);\n    }\n    let mut acc = std::hint::black_box(&buf).iter().fold(0u64, |a, b| a ^ b);\n    if depth > 0 {\n        acc ^= dirty_stack(depth - 1);\n    }\n    std::hint::black_box(acc)\n}\n\nfn gjk_poly(f: &libloading::Symbol<'_, FnGJK>, cap: &c2Capsule, poly: &c2Poly) -> (f32, c2v, c2v, i32) {\n    let (mut a, mut b, mut it) = (poison_v(1), poison_v(2), -12345i32);\n    let d = unsafe {\n        f(\n            cap as *const c2Capsule as *const c_void,\n            C2_TYPE_CAPSULE,\n            std::ptr::null(),\n            poly as *const c2Poly as *const c_void,\n            C2_TYPE_POLY,\n            std::ptr::null(),\n            &mut a,\n            &mut b,\n            0,\n            &mut it,\n            std::ptr::null_mut(),\n        )\n    };\n    (d, a, b, it)\n}\n\n/// The Rust side implements the zero-proxy model: a POLY operand behaves as the\n/// single point (0,0) with radius 0, so `c2GJK(capsule, POLY)` returns the distance\n/// from the capsule *segment* to the origin with `outB == (0,0)`.\n#[test]\nfn rust_poly_operand_is_the_zero_proxy() {\n    let l = libs();\n    let (_cf, rf) = l.get::<FnGJK>(\"c2GJK\");\n\n    // Closest point of the segment [(3,4),(5,6)] to (0,0) is (3,4), distance 5.\n    let cap = c2Capsule { a: v(3.0, 4.0), b: v(5.0, 6.0), r: 1.0 };\n    let mut poly = c2Poly::default();\n    poly.count = 5;\n    for i in 0..5 {\n        poly.verts[i] = v(10.0 + i as f32, 20.0 - i as f32);\n    }\n\n    let (rd, ra, rb, rit) = gjk_poly(&rf, &cap, &poly);\n    assert_eq!(rd, 5.0, \"Rust must report the segment-to-origin distance\");\n    assert_eq!(ra, v(3.0, 4.0), \"witness on A\");\n    assert_eq!(rb, v(0.0, 0.0), \"witness on B is the origin (zero proxy)\");\n    assert_eq!(rit, 0, \"terminates immediately\");\n}\n\n/// ...and it is *deterministic*: the same inputs give the same bytes no matter how\n/// dirty the stack below the caller's frame is. This is exactly the property the C\n/// library lacks.\n#[test]\nfn rust_poly_operand_is_deterministic_under_dirty_stack() {\n    let l = libs();\n    let (_cf, rf) = l.get::<FnGJK>(\"c2GJK\");\n    let cap = c2Capsule { a: v(3.0, 4.0), b: v(5.0, 6.0), r: 1.0 };\n    let poly = c2Poly::default();\n\n    let reference = gjk_poly(&rf, &cap, &poly);\n    for depth in [0u32, 1, 4, 16, 40] {\n        let sink = dirty_stack(depth);\n        let got = gjk_poly(&rf, &cap, &poly);\n        assert_eq!(\n            (got.0.to_bits(), got.1, got.2, got.3),\n            (reference.0.to_bits(), reference.1, reference.2, reference.3),\n            \"Rust c2GJK(POLY) changed after dirtying the stack (depth {depth}, sink {sink:x})\"\n        );\n    }\n}\n\n/// Document, rather than assert, the C library's garbage: print what it returns so\n/// the divergence is on the record, and prove it is *not* a function of its inputs\n/// by showing the same inputs give a value derived from a stack address.\n#[test]\nfn c_poly_operand_reads_uninitialised_stack() {\n    let l = libs();\n    let (cf, _rf) = l.get::<FnGJK>(\"c2GJK\");\n    let cap = c2Capsule { a: v(3.0, 4.0), b: v(5.0, 6.0), r: 1.0 };\n    let poly = c2Poly::default();\n\n    let (cd, ca, cb, cit) = gjk_poly(&cf, &cap, &poly);\n    println!(\"C   c2GJK(CAPSULE, POLY) -> d={cd} outA={ca:?} outB={cb:?} iters={cit}\");\n    println!(\"    outB bits = (0x{:08x}, 0x{:08x})\", cb.x.to_bits(), cb.y.to_bits());\n    println!(\"    -> reinterpreted as one 64-bit little-endian word: 0x{:016x}\",\n        ((cb.y.to_bits() as u64) << 32) | cb.x.to_bits() as u64);\n    println!(\"    a stack address on this machine looks like 0x00007f........\");\n\n    // The witness point on A is still correct (pA *is* initialised for a capsule),\n    // which pinpoints pB as the uninitialised operand.\n    assert_eq!(ca, v(3.0, 4.0), \"pA is initialised, so outA is meaningful\");\n\n    // No assertion on `cd` / `cb`: they are indeterminate. This test exists to\n    // document the UB, not to pin it down.\n    let _ = (cd, cb, cit);\n}\n\n/// Rust must never crash on the POLY path, however the polygon is shaped --\n/// including `count` values far outside 0..=8.\n#[test]\nfn rust_poly_path_never_crashes() {\n    let l = libs();\n    let (_cf, rf) = l.get::<FnGJK>(\"c2GJK\");\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(0x5EED_1234);\n    for trial in 0..200 {\n        let cap = c2Capsule { a: rng.vec_mixed(20.0), b: rng.vec_mixed(20.0), r: rng.f_mixed(3.0) };\n        let mut poly = c2Poly::default();\n        poly.count = match trial % 5 {\n            0 => 0,\n            1 => -7,\n            2 => 8,\n            3 => 4,\n            _ => rng.below(9) as i32,\n        };\n        for i in 0..8 {\n            poly.verts[i] = rng.vec_mixed(10.0);\n            poly.norms[i] = rng.vec_mixed(1.0);\n        }\n        let (mut a, mut b, mut it) = (c2v::default(), c2v::default(), 0i32);\n        let d = unsafe {\n            rf(\n                &cap as *const c2Capsule as *const c_void,\n                C2_TYPE_CAPSULE,\n                std::ptr::null(),\n                &poly as *const c2Poly as *const c_void,\n                C2_TYPE_POLY,\n                std::ptr::null(),\n                &mut a,\n                &mut b,\n                0,\n                &mut it,\n                std::ptr::null_mut(),\n            )\n        };\n        // Just needs to return; assert the out params were written at all.\n        assert!(it >= 0 && it <= 20, \"trial {trial}: iterations out of range: {it}\");\n        let _ = (d, a, b);\n    }\n}\n","userModified":false}}
