h be\",\n           \"  null; every one is null-checked.\",\n           \"* If `cache` is non-null it must point to a writable `c2GJKCache`, and its\",\n           \"  `iA`/`iB` entries must index vertices the proxy actually has\",\n           \"  (`1` for a circle, `2` for a capsule, `4` for an AABB). Out-of-range\",\n           \"  indices make the C original read uninitialised proxy slots.\"],\n \"c2PlaneAt\": [\"`p` must point to a valid, initialised `c2Poly`. `i` is used **unchecked**,\",\n               \"exactly as in C: values outside `0..8` read outside `p->verts` /\",\n               \"`p->norms`, and the caller is responsible for those bytes being mapped.\"],\n \"c2BBVerts\": [\"`out` must be valid for writes of **4** `c2v` values and `bb` must point to\",\n               \"a valid, initialised `c2AABB`. `bb` is not modified (it is `*mut` only\",\n               \"because the C signature is).\"],\n \"c2MakeProxy\": [\"`p` must point to a writable `c2Proxy`. `shape` must point to a shape\",\n                 \"matching `type_` -- a `c2Circle`, `c2AABB` or `c2Capsule`. For\",\n                 \"`C2_TYPE_POLY` or any out-of-range value neither pointer is\",\n                 \"dereferenced and `*p` is left completely untouched.\"],\n \"c2Support\": [\"`verts` must be valid for reads of `max(count, 1)` `c2v` values: note the\",\n               \"`max`, because the C original reads `verts[0]` **before** testing the loop\",\n               \"bound, so `verts[0]` must be readable even when `count <= 0`.\"],\n \"c2Norms\": [\"`verts` must be valid for reads and `norms` for writes of `count` `c2v`\",\n             \"values each. `count <= 0` touches neither. `verts` is not modified (it is\",\n             \"`*mut` only because the C signature is).\"],\n \"c2Collide\": [\"`m` must point to a writable `c2Manifold`. `A` must point to a shape\",\n               \"matching `typeA` and `B` one matching `typeB`; for `C2_TYPE_POLY` or any\",\n               \"out-of-range value the corresponding pointer is **not** dereferenced and\",\n               \"only `m->count = 0` is written. Shapes are read with\",\n               \"`read_unaligned`, so `A` and `B` need no particular alignment.\"],\n \"ptr_from_parts\": [\"No pointer arguments, but the returned pointer comes from `malloc(3)` and\",\n                    \"is **never freed** by this crate -- the caller owns it and must release it\",\n                    \"with `free(3)`, not with Rust's allocator. Returns null for\",\n                    \"`C2_TYPE_POLY` and any out-of-range value.\"],\n \"omni_manifold\": [\"`m` must point to a writable `c2Manifold`. Like the C original, this\",\n                   \"**leaks** both shapes it allocates with `ptr_from_parts`.\"],\n \"c2CircletoCircleManifold\": [\"`m` must point to a writable `c2Manifold`. Only `m->count` is written when\",\n                              \"the circles do not overlap; the other fields keep the caller's bytes.\"],\n \"c2CircletoAABBManifold\": [\"`m` must point to a writable `c2Manifold`. Only `m->count` is written when\",\n                            \"the circle is outside the box; the other fields keep the caller's bytes.\"],\n \"c2CircletoCapsuleManifold\": [\"`m` must point to a writable `c2Manifold`. Only `m->count` is written when\",\n                               \"the shapes do not overlap; the other fields keep the caller's bytes.\"],\n \"c2AABBtoAABBManifold\": [\"`m` must point to a writable `c2Manifold`. Only `m->count` is written when\",\n                          \"the boxes are separated on either axis; the other fields keep the\",\n                          \"caller's bytes.\"],\n \"c2CapsuletoPolyManifold\": [\"* `m` must point to a writable `c2Manifold` and `B` to a valid, initialised\",\n                             \"  `c2Poly`. `bx_ptr` may be null.\",\n                             \"* **`B->verts[-1]` is read** -- four bytes before the struct -- whenever\",\n                             \