{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ejgyc4e3wsr5f42b5kgv62ylquf3hr2td6hv47t6n6z2b3wcmvta","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four completion gates verified independently. Verification is complete.\n\n## What I found and fixed\n\nThe translation looked complete — 46/46 symbols already matched and the happy path passed — but the differential tests found **22 real bugs**, all in one blind spot.\n\n**The root cause:** `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` sets no `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE`, so the reference is compiled at **`-O0`**. The prior translation had *guessed* which SSE operand GCC uses as the `addss`/`mulss` **destination**, reasoning from an `-O2` mental model (vectorized `mulps`, PLT-forced register choices). At `-O0` the destination falls out of the load order instead, and 21 sites were backwards. Since the destination NaN wins when both operands are NaN, each wrong guess is a reachable difference in the returned NaN payload. I disassembled all 75 `addss`/`mulss` sites and read the truth off the instructions — e.g. `c2Dot` is really `add(mul(b.y,a.y), mul(a.x,b.x))`, with the two `mulss` picking *opposite* operands.\n\n**Bug 22 was a different species:** `c2AABBtoCapsuleManifold` builds a `c2Poly` as a local, and `c2CapsuletoPolyManifold` reads `B->verts[-1]` when a degenerate AABB makes every face normal NaN. That read lands in GCC's own frame, where `A` sits immediately before `p` — so `verts[-1] == (A.max.y, p.count)`. Rust's layout differed, so the whole manifold diverged. Fixed by pinning the adjacency with a `#[repr(C)]` frame struct.\n\n## The judgement call worth flagging\n\n`c2GJK` reads an **uninitialised `c2Proxy`** on every polygon path. I proved this is genuine UB, not a benign quirk: a fresh C driver segfaults *reproducibly* (exit 139), and in-process it returns literal stack addresses (`0x00007f89_3affe180`). The existing doc comment claimed the region \"reads back as all-zero\" — that was wrong.\n\nRather than write those paths off, I found that zeroing 8 KiB of stack immediately before the FFI call forces the C side into the all-zero state the Rust models, making them comparable byte-for-byte. That matters because it is the **only** route to the five `static` helpers (`c2Clip`, `c2SidePlanes`, `c2SidePlanesFromPoly`, `c2KeepDeep`, `c2Incident`) and to the `(AABB, CAPSULE)` pairs. The trick is order-sensitive — `zero_stack()` must be the last statement before the call, since even a tiny helper re-dirties the region — which is documented at the helper and was itself the cause of two intermediate failures I had to chase down.\n\n## Two caveats on my results\n\n- **`ptr_from_parts(POLY)` remains divergent** and is unfixable: C falls off the end of a non-`void` function and returns a stale register. Rust returns `NULL`. It's unobservable (`c2Collide` never dereferences it for POLY), and rows 5–9 verify that byte-for-byte across all 16 type pairs plus 7 out-of-range enum values.\n- **`ERRORS.md` row 27** (the `while (iter < 20)` cap) is verified only indirectly. `*iterations` is compared on every call, but a ~108K-call search never exceeded 5, so the cap — and the uninitialised `s.b.u` read it would enable — appears unreachable. I documented the histogram rather than claiming the row was exercised.\n\n**Results:** 105 tests / 10 binaries, green across 3 debug and 2 release runs. Release matters here — optimisation could have collapsed the NaN-selects in `fp.rs`, and it doesn't. `c_src/` is byte-identical to the original (I removed stray artifacts an early `cd` had dropped into `c_src/src/`). Findings are written up in `VERIFICATION.md`, and the false claims in the `lib.rs`/`fp.rs` module docs are corrected with the disassembly they should have been based on."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1779,"cache_read_input_tokens":476143,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1779,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"27d6de7a-57e2-4fbc-9590-8efa6a5bf865","uuid":"db4110e8-6360-4b98-b677-9ed5d87f533a","timestamp":"2026-08-20T13:01:25.144Z"}
